ation:** The discount is being applied twice - once in the original calculation `price * quantity * (1 - discount)` and again in the new line `total = total * (1 - discount)`. This will result in an incorrect total.\n\n3. **Misleading comment:** The comment \"# members get their discount\" is confusing because the discount is already being applied in the calculation.\n\n**Recommendation:**\n- Fix the condition to `quantity < 0` if you want to return 0 for negative quantities, or revert to `quantity > 0` if you want the original behavior.\n- Remove the duplicate discount application.\n- Remove or clarify the misleading comment.\n\n**Looks good:**\n- The function now rounds the result to 2 decimal places, which is good practice for currency calculations."},
